---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT, LINKS, withBase } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Support Qortium';
const description =
  'Qortium is maintained by one developer with real recurring costs. Voluntary support keeps releases, testing, and the Previewnet infrastructure running.';

const tiers = [
  {
    amount: '$3 / month',
    name: 'Keep it running',
    p: 'Helps cover the recurring cost of keeping the work active.',
  },
  {
    amount: '$8 / month',
    name: 'Share the monthly burn',
    p: 'Covers a meaningful share of tools, infrastructure, and maintenance.',
  },
  {
    amount: '$20 / month',
    name: 'Back the infrastructure',
    p: 'Materially reduces the monthly risk of running the seed nodes and gateway.',
  },
];

const boundaries = [
  {
    h: 'Everything stays open',
    p: 'No feature is paywalled, and nothing here becomes subscriber-only. Every repository stays open source under its existing license.',
  },
  {
    h: 'No roadmap control',
    p: 'Support does not buy priority over other users, influence over what gets built, or a private channel to me.',
  },
  {
    h: 'No private support tier',
    p: 'Bug reports and questions are handled the same way for everyone, in public, wherever they are filed.',
  },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: title,
  description,
  url: SUPPORT.pageUrl,
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/support" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-head">
        <h1>Support the work</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="lede measure">
        I&rsquo;m QuickMythril, and I maintain Qortium &mdash; the Core node, the
        Home desktop and Android app, the QDN apps, and the Previewnet seed
        nodes and gateway that keep it reachable. That work has real recurring
        costs. This page is how I make those costs visible and let people help
        cover them, without putting anything behind a paywall.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={SUPPORT.kofi}>Support on Ko-fi</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SUPPORT.liberapay}>Support on Liberapay</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What the money actually goes to</h2>
      <p class="muted measure">
        These are the recurring costs behind Qortium development and the public
        Previewnet infrastructure. I pay them out of pocket today. Amounts are
        approximate and change with exchange rates and provider pricing.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Cost</th>
              <th>What it covers</th>
              <th>Amount</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Regxa VPS</strong></td>
              <td>Previewnet seed node, QDN data, and the qortium.app gateway</td>
              <td>$15 / month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Netcup VPS</strong></td>
              <td>Second Previewnet seed node, for redundancy across providers</td>
              <td>about $7 / month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>AI development tools</strong></td>
              <td>
                Two assistant subscriptions used daily for research,
                implementation, review, testing, and documentation
              </td>
              <td>$212 / month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Connectivity</strong></td>
              <td>Phone and network access used for maintenance and testing</td>
              <td>$45 / month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>qortium.app domain</strong></td>
              <td>This website and the public gateway</td>
              <td>about €32 / year</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="muted measure">
        That comes to roughly <strong>$279 per month</strong>, plus the annual
        domain charge. The target for this page is <strong>$300 per month</strong>,
        which leaves a small margin for processing fees and currency
        conversion. Anything beyond that goes to the same place the rest does:
        release stability, testing, and reducing maintenance debt.
      </p>
      <p class="muted measure">
        The two AI subscriptions are the largest line by far, and I list them
        deliberately rather than hiding them in &ldquo;tools.&rdquo; They are
        general-purpose developer tools I use across all of this work, not
        dedicated project infrastructure. AI-assisted changes go through the
        same review and testing as everything else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Suggested amounts</h2>
      <p class="muted measure">
        Any amount helps, and these are only suggestions &mdash; both platforms
        below let you choose your own. The first milestone is small and
        concrete: at <strong>$5 per month</strong> the second seed node moves to
        a larger plan, which directly addresses the memory pressure that has
        taken it down before.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {tiers.map((t) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{t.amount}</h3>
            <p><strong>{t.name}</strong></p>
            <p class="muted">{t.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ways to support</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Ko-fi</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            One-time or monthly support, paid through PayPal. Monthly support
            renews automatically through PayPal&rsquo;s Automatic Payments.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href={SUPPORT.kofi}>Open Ko-fi</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Liberapay</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Open-source funding platform that takes no cut &mdash; only the
            payment processor&rsquo;s fee applies. Payments currently run
            through PayPal, which asks you to confirm each renewal rather than
            charging automatically.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SUPPORT.liberapay}>Open Liberapay</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted measure">
        A direct card option is being set up and will appear here once it is
        live. If you would rather support the work another way, email me at the
        address below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What support does and does not buy</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {boundaries.map((c) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{c.h}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{c.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Billing, cancellation, and refunds</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="muted">
          <strong>Recurring support</strong> is billed once a month by the
          platform you choose, starting on the day you sign up, and continues
          until you cancel.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          <strong>Cancelling</strong> is done in your own account on that
          platform, at any time, without contacting me. Cancellation stops
          future payments; the period you have already paid for is not
          prorated.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          <strong>Refunds:</strong> if you were charged by mistake, changed your
          mind, or something on this page was not what you expected, email me
          within 30 days of the payment and I will refund it in full. No
          explanation required. Refunds go back to the payment method you used
          and typically take 5&ndash;10 business days to appear.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          <strong>Currency:</strong> all amounts on this page are in US dollars
          unless stated otherwise. Your bank may apply its own conversion rate
          and fees if you pay in another currency.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="muted">
          Questions about supporting this work, billing, or refunds go to
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a>. I answer
          personally, usually within a few days.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          For bugs and feature requests, please use the issue tracker on the
          relevant repository instead &mdash; it keeps the discussion public and
          searchable for everyone else.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={LINKS.siteRepo}>Source for this site</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Privacy and your data</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="muted">
          Payments are handled entirely by the platform you choose. I never see
          or store your card number, bank details, or billing address &mdash;
          those stay with the payment provider. What I do see is the name or
          handle you supported under, the amount, and any message you send with
          it.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          If you email me, I keep that email to reply to you and for my own
          records of payments and refunds. I do not sell, rent, or share
          supporter information with anyone, and I do not send marketing email.
          Ask me to delete your details and I will, except where I have to keep
          a record of a payment.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          This website sets no tracking cookies and runs no analytics. Version
          numbers shown on some pages are fetched from GitHub when the page
          loads, which means GitHub sees that request.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Terms</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="muted">
          Support on this page is <strong>voluntary</strong>. It is not a
          purchase of software, a licence, a service contract, or a promise that
          any particular feature will be built or that the network will keep
          running. Qortium is preview software, provided as-is, under the open
          source licences in its repositories.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Support is <strong>not a tax-deductible charitable donation</strong>.
          I am an individual developer, not a registered charity, and nothing
          here should be treated as a donation to a non-profit.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Qortium is an independent project. It is not Qortal, and it is not
          affiliated with or endorsed by the Qortal project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
